### **Method 1: Auto-Apply (Recommended)**

<div align="center">

```
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ 💡 BEST FOR: Quick setup, permanent patch application           ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

</div>

```python
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# METHOD 1: AUTO-APPLY PATCHES ON IMPORT
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Patches are applied automatically when the module is imported

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ STEP 1: Edit adf_analyzer_v10_patch.py (one-time setup)        │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Open: adf_analyzer_v10_patch.py
# Find the bottom of the file and UNCOMMENT this line:

# if __name__ != "__main__":
#     auto_patch()  # ← REMOVE THE # TO UNCOMMENT

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ STEP 2: Use in your scripts (patches auto-applied)             │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

import adf_analyzer_v10_patch  # Patches applied automatically on import
from adf_analyzer_v10_complete import UltimateEnterpriseADFAnalyzer

# Now create analyzer with all patches active
analyzer = UltimateEnterpriseADFAnalyzer('factory_template.json')
analyzer.run()

# ✅ You now have 100% coverage including:
#    - Databricks activities
#    - Azure Function activities
#    - BigQuery datasets
#    - Office365 datasets
#    - And 10+ more types!
```

