### **Top 10 Best Practices**

<div align="center">

```
╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║                                                                   ║
║         🏆 TOP 10 BEST PRACTICES FOR ADF ANALYZER                 ║
║                                                                   ║
╠═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║                                                                   ║
║  1️⃣  RUN ANALYSIS REGULARLY                                       ║
║     • Weekly: For active development                             ║
║     • Pre-deployment: ALWAYS                                     ║
║     • Post-deployment: Verify changes                            ║
║                                                                   ║
║  2️⃣  ZERO CIRCULAR DEPENDENCIES POLICY                            ║
║     • Never deploy with circular dependencies                    ║
║     • Fix immediately if found                                   ║
║     • Add to CI/CD gates                                         ║
║                                                                   ║
║  3️⃣  KEEP ORPHANED RESOURCES < 5%                                 ║
║     • Review monthly                                             ║
║     • Delete confirmed orphans                                   ║
║     • Document "kept for future use" resources                   ║
║                                                                   ║
║  4️⃣  REVIEW IMPACT ANALYSIS BEFORE CHANGES                        ║
║     • Check CRITICAL impact pipelines                            ║
║     • Understand blast radius                                    ║
║     • Plan rollback strategy                                     ║
║                                                                   ║
║  5️⃣  VERSION CONTROL ANALYSIS REPORTS                             ║
║     • Commit Excel files to Git                                  ║
║     • Track changes over time                                    ║
║     • Compare before/after deployments                           ║
║                                                                   ║
║  6️⃣  INTEGRATE WITH CI/CD PIPELINE                                ║
║     • Run on every PR                                            ║
║     • Block deployment if circular deps found                    ║
║     • Auto-generate documentation                                ║
║                                                                   ║
║  7️⃣  DOCUMENT CRITICAL PIPELINES                                  ║
║     • Use Impact Analysis to identify                            ║
║     • Create runbooks for CRITICAL impact                        ║
║     • Update documentation regularly                             ║
║                                                                   ║
║  8️⃣  USE NAMING CONVENTIONS                                       ║
║     • Consistent pipeline naming                                 ║
║     • Folder organization                                        ║
║     • Makes analysis more readable                               ║
║                                                                   ║
║  9️⃣  MONITOR COMPLEXITY SCORES                                    ║
║     • Track over time                                            ║
║     • Refactor if score > 100                                    ║
║     • Simplify complex pipelines                                 ║
║                                                                   ║
║  🔟  SHARE REPORTS WITH TEAM                                      ║
║     • Weekly review meetings                                     ║
║     • Highlight key findings                                     ║
║     • Assign action items                                        ║
║                                                                   ║
╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

</div>

### **Tips for Large Factories (1000+ Pipelines)**

<table>
<tr>
<td width="50%">

**Performance Optimization:**

1. ⚡ Use `--no-discovery` for faster parsing
2. 🔄 Split analysis by folder (analyze subsets)
3. 💾 Increase memory (16-32 GB RAM recommended)
4. 🌙 Run overnight (can take 5-10 minutes)

</td>
<td width="50%">

**UX Tips:**

5. 🔍 Use Excel filters extensively
6. 📊 Focus on Summary first
7. 🎯 Drill down to details as needed
8. 📝 Create custom views/filters

</td>
</tr>
</table>

### **Common Pitfalls to Avoid**

<div align="center">

```
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ ⚠️ COMMON PITFALLS TO AVOID                                     ║
╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║                                                                  ║
║ ❌ Deploying with circular dependencies                         ║
║    → Always run pre-deployment check                            ║
║                                                                  ║
║ ❌ Ignoring orphaned resources                                  ║
║    → Clean up monthly, don't let them accumulate                ║
║                                                                  ║
║ ❌ Not checking impact before changes                           ║
║    → Review ImpactAnalysis sheet first                          ║
║                                                                  ║
║ ❌ Running analyzer only when issues occur                      ║
║    → Make it part of regular workflow                           ║
║                                                                  ║
║ ❌ Not version controlling analysis reports                     ║
║    → Commit to Git to track changes over time                   ║
║                                                                  ║
║ ❌ Manual scrolling through large Excel files                   ║
║    → Use filters and search functionality                       ║
║                                                                  ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

</div>

