## **6.1 RESOURCE PARSING (10 TYPES)**

### **Feature At A Glance**

<table>
<tr>
<td width="60%">

#### **What It Does**

The Resource Parser automatically detects and classifies all Azure Data Factory resources from ARM templates into 10 distinct types. Each resource type has specialized parsing logic to extract relevant properties.

**Key Capabilities:**
- ✅ **Auto-Detection** - Pattern matching on resource type strings
- ✅ **10 Resource Types** - Complete ADF resource coverage
- ✅ **O(1) Lookup** - Hash-based registry for instant access
- ✅ **Property Extraction** - Type-specific property parsing
- ✅ **Error Recovery** - Graceful handling of malformed resources

</td>
<td width="40%">

**Supported Types:**

| Type | Count (typical) |
|:-----|:---------------:|
| Pipelines | 45 |
| DataFlows | 15 |
| Datasets | 89 |
| LinkedServices | 12 |
| Triggers | 8 |
| IntegrationRuntimes | 3 |
| Credentials | 2 |
| ManagedVNets | 1 |
| PrivateEndpoints | 2 |
| GlobalParameters | 3 |

</td>
</tr>
</table>

### **Resource Type Detection Flow**

```mermaid
%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': { 'primaryColor':'#e3f2fd'}}}%%
graph TB
    START["📥 ARM Template<br/><small>resources array</small>"] --> ITERATE["🔄 Iterate Each Resource"]
    
    ITERATE --> EXTRACT["📋 Extract resource.type"]
    
    EXTRACT --> DETECT{{"🔍 Type Detection<br/><small>String Matching</small>"}}
    
    DETECT -->|"'pipelines'"| R1["⚙️ PIPELINE"]
    DETECT -->|"'dataflows'"| R2["🌊 DATAFLOW"]
    DETECT -->|"'datasets'"| R3["📊 DATASET"]
    DETECT -->|"'linkedservices'"| R4["🔗 LINKED_SERVICE"]
    DETECT -->|"'triggers'"| R5["⏰ TRIGGER"]
    DETECT -->|"'integrationruntimes'"| R6["🖥️ INTEGRATION_RUNTIME"]
    DETECT -->|"'credentials'"| R7["🔐 CREDENTIAL"]
    DETECT -->|"'managedvirtualnetworks'"| R8["🌐 MANAGED_VNET"]
    DETECT -->|"'managedprivateendpoints'"| R9["🔒 MANAGED_PRIVATE_ENDPOINT"]
    DETECT -->|"'globalparameters'"| R10["⚙️ GLOBAL_PARAMETER"]
    
    R1 --> STORE1["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['pipelines']</small>"]
    R2 --> STORE2["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['dataflows']</small>"]
    R3 --> STORE3["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['datasets']</small>"]
    R4 --> STORE4["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['linkedServices']</small>"]
    R5 --> STORE5["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['triggers']</small>"]
    R6 --> STORE6["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['integrationRuntimes']</small>"]
    R7 --> STORE7["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['credentials']</small>"]
    R8 --> STORE8["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['managedVirtualNetworks']</small>"]
    R9 --> STORE9["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['managedPrivateEndpoints']</small>"]
    R10 --> STORE10["📦 Store in<br/><small>resources['globalParameters']</small>"]
    
    STORE1 --> REGISTRY["🗂️ Central Resource Registry<br/><small>O(1) Access</small>"]
    STORE2 --> REGISTRY
    STORE3 --> REGISTRY
    STORE4 --> REGISTRY
    STORE5 --> REGISTRY
    STORE6 --> REGISTRY
    STORE7 --> REGISTRY
    STORE8 --> REGISTRY
    STORE9 --> REGISTRY
    STORE10 --> REGISTRY
    
    REGISTRY --> NEXT["✅ Ready for Parsing"]
    
    classDef startStyle fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2,stroke-width:2px
    classDef detectStyle fill:#fff9c4,stroke:#f57f17,stroke-width:3px
    classDef storeStyle fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#6a1b9a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef registryStyle fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:3px
    
    class START startStyle
    class DETECT detectStyle
    class STORE1,STORE2,STORE3,STORE4,STORE5,STORE6,STORE7,STORE8,STORE9,STORE10 storeStyle
    class REGISTRY registryStyle
```

