## **6.8 NESTED ACTIVITY HANDLING**

### **Feature At A Glance**

<table>
<tr>
<td width="60%">

#### **What It Does**

Recursively parses nested activities (ForEach, IfCondition, Switch, Until) while maintaining correct sequence numbers and depth tracking.

**Key Capabilities:**
- ✅ **Recursive Parsing** - Handles unlimited nesting (with depth limit)
- ✅ **Depth Protection** - MAX_DEPTH=20 prevents stack overflow
- ✅ **Sequence Tracking** - Maintains execution order across nesting
- ✅ **4 Container Types** - ForEach, IfCondition, Switch, Until
- ✅ **Parent Tracking** - Full path to root activity

</td>
<td width="40%">

**Typical Nesting:**

| Depth | Common | Max Seen |
|:------|:------:|:--------:|
| **0** | 70% | - |
| **1** | 20% | - |
| **2** | 8% | - |
| **3-5** | 2% | 15 |

**Limit:** 20 levels (safety)

</td>
</tr>
</table>

### **Recursive Parsing Architecture**

```mermaid
%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': { 'primaryColor':'#e3f2fd'}}}%%
graph TD
    START["parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>activities, pipeline, parent, depth, seq</small>"] --> CHECK{{"depth ><br/>MAX_DEPTH?"}}
    
    CHECK -->|"Yes ❌"| ERROR["🔴 Error:<br/><small>Max depth exceeded</small><br/><small>Log error & return seq</small>"]
    CHECK -->|"No ✅"| LOOP{{"More<br/>Activities?"}}
    
    LOOP -->|"Yes"| PARSE["🔍 parse_activity()<br/><small>current_activity</small>"]
    LOOP -->|"No"| RETURN["↩️ Return final seq"]
    
    PARSE --> SEQ["🔢 seq += 1"]
    
    SEQ --> TYPE{{"🎯 Activity<br/>Type?"}}
    
    TYPE -->|"ForEach"| FOREACH["🔁 Get nested activities"]
    TYPE -->|"IfCondition"| IF["❓ Get true/false branches"]
    TYPE -->|"Switch"| SWITCH["🔀 Get case branches"]
    TYPE -->|"Until"| UNTIL["🔄 Get loop activities"]
    TYPE -->|"Other"| LOOP
    
    FOREACH --> RECURSE1["🔄 parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>RECURSIVE CALL</small><br/><small>depth + 1</small>"]
    IF --> RECURSE2["🔄 parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>TRUE branch, depth + 1</small>"]
    IF --> RECURSE3["🔄 parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>FALSE branch, depth + 1</small>"]
    SWITCH --> RECURSE4["🔄 parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>CASE branches, depth + 1</small>"]
    SWITCH --> RECURSE5["🔄 parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>DEFAULT branch, depth + 1</small>"]
    UNTIL --> RECURSE6["🔄 parse_nested_activities()<br/><small>LOOP activities, depth + 1</small>"]
    
    RECURSE1 --> UPDATE["🔄 Update seq<br/><small>from recursion</small>"]
    RECURSE2 --> UPDATE
    RECURSE3 --> UPDATE
    RECURSE4 --> UPDATE
    RECURSE5 --> UPDATE
    RECURSE6 --> UPDATE
    
    UPDATE --> LOOP
    
    ERROR --> RETURN
    
    classDef startStyle fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2,stroke-width:2px
    classDef checkStyle fill:#fff9c4,stroke:#f57f17,stroke-width:2px
    classDef typeStyle fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#6a1b9a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef recurseStyle fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px
    classDef returnStyle fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px
    
    class START startStyle
    class CHECK,LOOP checkStyle
    class TYPE typeStyle
    class RECURSE1,RECURSE2,RECURSE3,RECURSE4,RECURSE5,RECURSE6 recurseStyle
    class RETURN returnStyle
```

### **Nested Structure Example**

```mermaid
%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': { 'primaryColor':'#e3f2fd'}}}%%
graph TD
    PL["⚙️ Pipeline: PL_Master<br/><small>Seq: 1, Depth: 0</small>"] --> A1["🔁 ForEach_Customers<br/><small>Seq: 1, Depth: 0, Parent: ''</small>"]
    
    A1 --> N1["📋 Copy_CustomerData<br/><small>Seq: 2, Depth: 1</small><br/><small>Parent: ForEach_Customers</small>"]
    
    A1 --> N2["❓ IfCondition_ValidCustomer<br/><small>Seq: 3, Depth: 1</small><br/><small>Parent: ForEach_Customers</small>"]
    
    N2 --> N3["🌊 ExecuteDataFlow_Transform<br/><small>Seq: 4, Depth: 2</small><br/><small>Parent: IfCondition→TRUE</small>"]
    
    N2 --> N4["❌ Fail_InvalidCustomer<br/><small>Seq: 5, Depth: 2</small><br/><small>Parent: IfCondition→FALSE</small>"]
    
    A1 --> NEXT["⏭️ Continue: Seq: 6"]
    
    PL --> A2["⏱️ Wait_5Minutes<br/><small>Seq: 6, Depth: 0, Parent: ''</small>"]
    
    classDef pipelineStyle fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2,stroke-width:3px
    classDef containerStyle fill:#fff9c4,stroke:#f57f17,stroke-width:2px
    classDef nestedStyle fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#6a1b9a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef trueStyle fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px
    classDef falseStyle fill:#ffebee,stroke:#c62828,stroke-width:2px
    
    class PL pipelineStyle
    class A1,N2 containerStyle
    class N1 nestedStyle
    class N3 trueStyle
    class N4 falseStyle
```

### **Sequence=0 Bug Fix**

<div align="center">

```
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ 🐛 CRITICAL BUG FIXED IN v10.0                                   ║
╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║ Bug: Sequence=0 treated as False in conditional checks          ║
║ Impact: First activity in pipeline lost in dependencies         ║
║ Fix: Explicit None checking instead of truthy evaluation        ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

</div>

<details>
<summary><b>🔍 Click to view the fix</b></summary>

```python
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BUG IN v9.2: Sequence=0 treated as False
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# v9.2 (BROKEN):
if from_seq and to_seq:  # ❌ Fails when seq=0
    sequence_flow = f"{from_seq}→{to_seq}"
else:
    sequence_flow = 'UNKNOWN'

# Example:
# Activity 1: seq=0 (first activity)
# Activity 2: seq=1
# Result: from_seq=0 is False, so sequence_flow='UNKNOWN' ❌

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# FIX IN v10.0: Explicit None checking
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# v10.0 (FIXED):
if from_seq is not None and to_seq is not None:  # ✅ Handles 0 correctly
    sequence_flow = f"{from_seq}→{to_seq}"
else:
    sequence_flow = 'UNKNOWN'

# ✅ Now seq=0 is correctly recognized as a valid sequence number
```

</details>

### **Recursion Depth Protection**

<table>
<tr>
<td width="60%">

**Configuration:**

```python
class Config:
    MAX_ACTIVITY_DEPTH = 20  # Configurable
    
    # Real-world observations:
    # - Typical: 3-5 levels
    # - Complex: 8-10 levels
    # - Maximum seen: 15 levels
    # - Safety limit: 20 (margin)
```

**Protection Mechanism:**
- Check depth before recursion
- Log error if MAX_DEPTH exceeded
- Return gracefully (no crash)
- Continue parsing other activities

</td>
<td width="40%">

```mermaid
%%{init: {'theme':'base'}}%%
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> CheckDepth: parse(depth)
    
    CheckDepth --> Continue: depth < 20
    CheckDepth --> Error: depth >= 20
    
    Continue --> ParseActivity
    
    ParseActivity --> HasNested: Check nested
    
    HasNested --> Recurse: depth+1
    HasNested --> Next: No nesting
    
    Recurse --> CheckDepth
    
    Next --> [*]: Done
    
    Error --> Log: Log error
    Log --> [*]: Stop recursion
```

</td>
</tr>
</table>

<div align="center">

```
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ 💡 NESTED ACTIVITY INSIGHTS                                      ║
╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║ • Recursion: Handles unlimited nesting with depth protection    ║
║ • Sequence: Maintains correct execution order across levels     ║
║ • Parent Tracking: Full path for drill-down analysis            ║
║ • Performance: O(N) where N = total activities                  ║
║ • Safety: MAX_DEPTH=20 prevents stack overflow                  ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

</div>

